Subject: [PATCH 05/21] EXEC-MU-ACCOUNTS fix round (plans): the shell shows
 refusals in words, lands a non-admin account on the Terminal, follows a
 change of plan and a session ended under a frame

Re-check R2-14, R2-30: edge-client.js ApiError carries the person's words as its message and the code as .code (the
export's busy check reads the code); a sign-in lands on the Monitor only for an account whose access holds it, else on
the Terminal. R2-16, R2-31: the shell reads its session again (and the model list and preferences) when
X-Edge-Entitlements changes on its own answers or in a frame's broadcast (shared module onVersion); MFA_REQUIRED
carries the principal's version and mfa_enrolled. R2-17: a page whose own session ended (401) says so on the channel and
to its parent (onSignedOut), and the shell reads its session and goes to sign-in on a 401.

Tests whose landing expectation follows the Terminal decision wait for the landing page instead of the Monitor's
composer (test_c2web_browser signed_in and W1, e2e_people register, test_c2_e2e_people, test_auth_pages_live).

