From 78455b93bce3e343a60aa888086854fdfeed0fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:00:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/21] EXEC-MU-ACCOUNTS fix round (plans): every plan limit
 answers one code, LIMIT_REACHED naming its capability key

Re-check R2-39 (CONTRACT.md section 3): the saved-item caps (layouts, presets, places with drawings, saved screens and
metrics, watchlists, tickers per list, indicators) answered 422 LIMIT_EXCEEDED with a local name, which the shared module
never treats as a plan refusal. errors.plan_cap answers them 403 LIMIT_REACHED with details.limit the capability key,
allowed and needed, in the plan's words (errors.words; a capability key is a plan limit even before the catalog's names
load); 403 because waiting frees nothing, while the backtest queue, which frees itself, stays 429 with Retry-After. An
empty indicator choice is INVALID_INPUT, not a cap. The Terminal's drawings lock only on the kinds upgrade and mfa, never
on a cap. The tests that locked the old code follow it, as the finding asks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015yBxadqbqnpdpSwmfCDQca
